public class AccountFrozenException extends AppException {
    private final String accountId;
    private final String frozenReason;
    private final java.time.Instant frozenAt;
    private final boolean canAppeal;

    public AccountFrozenException(String accountId, String frozenReason,
                                   java.time.Instant frozenAt, boolean canAppeal) {
        super('ACCOUNT_FROZEN',
            String.format('Account %s is frozen (reason: %s, since: %s)',
                accountId, frozenReason, frozenAt));
        this.accountId    = accountId;
        this.frozenReason = frozenReason;
        this.frozenAt     = frozenAt;
        this.canAppeal    = canAppeal;
    }
    // Getters for all fields...
}
Key design decisions: (1) Extends AppException (unchecked) — callers don't need try-catch. (2) Carries accountId for logging. (3) Carries frozenReason — enables targeted user messaging. (4) Carries frozenAt — supports 'frozen for X days' display. (5) Carries canAppeal — drives UI decision.

